WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Why can cancer escape a targeted treatment?

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:10.375
Figure 1A contrasts a target-positive cell with a target-negative cell.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.750
The CAR binding domain recognises a particular target antigen.

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:22.125
Target loss can undermine recognition by a single-target CAR.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.500
This resistance mechanism is called antigen escape.

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:33.875
Multiple targets are one strategy; relapse prevention is not guaranteed.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:41.250
A qualitative review schematic, not a measured treatment comparison.

